<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/su_verified_6ed52cdf724db04223b4d1c2e62f3c35f6b42bc19bc5e3198277d681d47e1eb9_table_24/e_0007> <http://digistrucmed.org/entityType> <http://digistrucmed.org/entity-type/VALUE> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/su_verified_6ed52cdf724db04223b4d1c2e62f3c35f6b42bc19bc5e3198277d681d47e1eb9_table_24/tu_0002> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "In patients with chronic or recurrent hyperkalaemia not on maximal tolerated guideline-recommended target dose of RAAS inhibitors, an approved $K^+$ -lowering agent may be initiated as soon as confirmed $K^+$ levels are $>5.0$ mEq/L. Closely monitor $K^+$ levels. Maintain treatment unless alternative treatable aetiology is identified. RAAS inhibitors should be optimized when $K^+$ levels are $<5.0$ mEq/L." .
